      '## 1. What is Modern Headless CMS Architecture? The Decoupled Paradigm Shift',
      'In a traditional monolithic CMS, the "head" (the frontend presentation layer: HTML, CSS, JavaScript) is inextricably linked to the "body" (the database, user management, and content authoring backend). Every time an end user visits a URL, the server queries MySQL, compiles PHP templates, executes dozens of plugins, and serves the resulting HTML.',
      'By contrast, **headless CMS architecture** completely severs this link. The CMS functions purely as a content repository accessible via authenticated APIs (GraphQL or REST). The frontend is a high-performance web application (built with React, Next.js, or Astro) running on distributed serverless edge networks like Cloudflare, Vercel, or AWS CloudFront.',
      'The table below illustrates the stark technical divergence between monolithic systems and modern headless ecosystems:',
      '| Infrastructure Vector | Monolithic CMS (Legacy WP/Drupal) | Enterprise Headless CMS Architecture |',
      '| :--- | :--- | :--- |',
